 # Live sources consulted
 
-Replace this placeholder with the live Broadcom sources used for the architecture.
+- **VMware by Broadcom Compatibility Guide** — https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: the current guide is the hardware compatibility authority for VCF and vSphere server, CPU, I/O, and storage targets represented by the snapshot's supported-topology screening.
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability?col=1 — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: product-version interoperability must be checked by product and release before accepting the snapshot's target component transitions.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: VCF 5.2.x can upgrade to 9.1 through the lifecycle workflow after VCF Operations, and VCF Management Services plus the centralized license server are mandatory.
+- **Certificate Requirements for VCF Operations for Networks in VCF 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/424807 — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: FQDN and IP SAN remediation is a pre-upgrade gate for Operations for Networks 6.14.
+- **vCenter Upgrade to 9.1 fails with NetFlow enabled on DVS Uplink Portgroups pre-check error** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/441813/vcenter-upgrade-to-91-fails-with-netflow.html — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: VCF Operations for Networks 9.1 must precede the vCenter 9.1 upgrade.
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with the versions of its constituent products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html — Consulted: 2026-08-14 — Fact used: the VCF 5.2.1 source BOM contains the inventory's vCenter, ESXi, NSX, and Aria Suite Lifecycle builds.
